\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  O God, Thou art my dearest father,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Who provides me with all my needs,
\par  'cause of Thy grace, when I take my breath,
\par My life is fully in Thine hands,
\par 'Tis Thou that brought me here on earth,
\par  Thou lovest and carest for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Grant that my bodily requirements,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And all that's pleasant to the flesh,
\par Draw me not into some transgression,
\par And thence into tribulation,
\par Make me keep Thy precepts in mind
\par And me to keep Thy Laws aright
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. Make me yield not to fleshly desires,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And make me hate all forms of lust,
\par Cast evil thinking away from me,
\par And unpleasant acts from my ears,
\par So that satan and all his snares,
\par May fail to trap and destroy me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. May my heart be rid of mischief, and
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Then turned into Thy dwelling place,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  Father, make my ears and all my eyes,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Even, my mouth and tongue as well,
\par  And all that belong unto me.
\par  Be thine to worship you always.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

